|ID = 690
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Child of Destiny Phono
|name2 = King of Destiny Phonoa
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''King of Destiny Phonoa''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Phono's normal form has an immense amount of DPS for their range and is decently stackable as well, giving them usage all across the game. Against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless enemies]], this unit is not recommended, as their DPS is very low without the [[Massive Damage]] effect. Phono's LD ability contributes to their effectiveness on the battlefield as well: they have an immense reach of up to 600 range, which gives them very good area denial and piercing range for their standing range. This makes Phono one of the only spammable units that is able to snipe backliners, a very valuable role. Overall, a very surprising normal form, as the other [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] exclusives do not necessarily have a useful one.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
In their evolved form, Phonoa has much longer reach, higher DPS and better survivability than the normal form in exchange for spammability. Phonoa's standing range is immense, at 600. This is the same standing range as [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Radiant Aphrodite]]. The average DPS for a backliner with range/reach around Aphrodite's is approximately 3.4k, but Phonoa blows this out of the water with a whopping '''11.3k effective''' DPS, effective from ranges 450-800. If this wasn't enough, they also have an immense '''5.6k effective''' DPS from ranges 800-1000 and 250-450. This means they can reach up to 1000 range with more than 5.2k average DPS, almost double Aphrodite's. In addition, they also have [[Immune to Waves|Wave]]/[[Immune to Surge|Surge immunity]], giving them relevance in newer stages and endgame, as well as a small range of 590-600 in which their full power of '''17k''' DPS is unleashed.

Of course, they do have a few weaknesses. Being an UBERFEST exclusive, their DPS against traitless enemies is unsatisfactory. [[Curse]] can even simply remove their impact on the field if they get hit. Their health is also not great, although they do tend to survive with their Immunities to Waves and Surges. Maximizing their DPS also proves to be difficult as only tiny segments of the multi-hits actually overlap. However, all of these are not massive flaws and can be worked around with the right strategy.

{{Job|Classification = Midranger & Sniper|EvolvedClass = Super-Backliner & Sniper|TrueClass=|UltraClass=}}

